{"uncertainty": 0.27, "outcome": "Wrote the RTL for the parameterizable synchronous FIFO (sync_fifo.v) and its self-checking testbench (sync_fifo_tb.v). The design follows the approved microarchitecture: an explicit occupancy counter, pointers that wrap at LAST, and a first-word fall-through read port. The testbench checks a DEPTH 8 x WIDTH 8 FIFO and a DEPTH 5 x WIDTH 12 FIFO against reference queues on every cycle. Lint, simulation and synthesis results are still pending: the platform runs them, not me.", "artifacts": [{"kind": "design_note", "title": "Traceability of sync_fifo RTL to its specifications", "summary": "Serves [requirement:req-d57ae7630b]. Ports, parameters, the overflow and underflow policy (drop or ignore, gated by the flags), first-word fall-through, and synchronous active-low reset all follow [artifact:prj-89e77b6204.interface-spec.a1]. Storage that is not reset, wrap-compare pointers of $clog2(DEPTH) bits, a counter of $clog2(DEPTH+1) bits, wr_acc/rd_acc gating with no read-to-write path, and rd_data = mem[rd_ptr] follow [artifact:prj-89e77b6204.microarchitecture.a1], which was reviewed under [evidence:prj-89e77b6204.microarchitecture.e1]."}], "files": [{"path": "sync_fifo.v", "kind": "rtl_source", "title": "sync_fifo RTL", "summary": "Parameterizable synchronous FIFO (DEPTH >= 2, any value, not only powers of two; WIDTH >= 1) implementing [artifact:prj-89e77b6204.microarchitecture.a1] for [requirement:req-d57ae7630b]. full, empty and count are compares on a register, so none depends combinationally on an input. Reset clears the pointers and the count only. Design-intent assertions sit under ifdef FORMAL: flag consistency, count and pointer range, the reset state, count moving only by accepted requests, and a write while full or a read while empty changing nothing on its side.", "entry": "sync_fifo"}, {"path": "sync_fifo_tb.v", "kind": "testbench", "title": "sync_fifo self-checking testbench", "summary": "Drives two FIFOs from one stimulus: DEPTH 8 x WIDTH 8 and DEPTH 5 x WIDTH 12, as [artifact:prj-89e77b6204.microarchitecture.a1] plans. Each cycle it checks count, full, empty and rd_data against a reference queue, as section 7 of [artifact:prj-89e77b6204.interface-spec.a1] requires. Stimulus is a directed phase followed by eight segments of biased random traffic with occasional resets. Coverage counters fail the run if any listed corner case is missed: full, write while full, drain to empty, read while empty, write and read together when empty, full and in between, pointer wrap, and reset during traffic. Failures use $error. The NIRMAAN-SIM verdict is printed once, just before $finish.", "entry": "sync_fifo_tb"}], "tool_runs": [], "claims": ["The RTL is intended to be clean under Verilator --lint-only -Wall at the default parameters. This has not been run or verified.", "The testbench is intended to pass under Icarus Verilog (SystemVerilog mode, for $error) and under Verilator with timing support. This has not been run or verified.", "The design is intended to synthesize in Yosys without latches: every register is in a clocked block and there is no combinational always block. This has not been run or verified.", "The ifdef FORMAL assertions have not been exercised by any proof, because this task submits no formal_spec file."], "escalation": null, "notes": "Decisions to record:\n(1) No formal_spec is submitted. The task's expected outputs are rtl_source and testbench only, so the SymbiYosys jobs that section 6 of the microarchitecture plans (sync_fifo.sby and sync_fifo_depth5.sby) are left to a formal task. The ifdef FORMAL block in the RTL is design intent only. It omits the pointer-distance invariant and the property for a slot chosen by the solver, which an unbounded proof will need. These are deviations from the verification plan and are recorded here so they are not silent.\n(2) sync_fifo_tb_fail.v, the negative-path testbench, is not delivered. The simulator takes its top from the first testbench file only.\n(3) Widths are derived from localparam integer copies of the parameters through part-selects, to avoid width warnings in Verilator -Wall.\n(4) The testbench drives and checks on the falling edge and updates its models after the rising edge. It uses a deterministic xorshift generator so that results are reproducible across simulators."}

=== FILE: sync_fifo.v ===
// sync_fifo: parameterizable synchronous FIFO, first-word fall-through.
// Implements microarchitecture.md (explicit occupancy counter, wrap-compare
// pointers, combinational read of the oldest slot).
`default_nettype none

module sync_fifo #(
    parameter integer DEPTH = 8,
    parameter integer WIDTH = 8
) (
    input  wire                       clk,
    input  wire                       rst_n,
    input  wire                       wr_en,
    input  wire [WIDTH-1:0]           wr_data,
    output wire                       full,
    input  wire                       rd_en,
    output wire [WIDTH-1:0]           rd_data,
    output wire                       empty,
    output wire [$clog2(DEPTH+1)-1:0] count
);

    localparam integer AW      = $clog2(DEPTH);
    localparam integer CW      = $clog2(DEPTH + 1);
    localparam integer LAST_I  = DEPTH - 1;
    localparam integer DEPTH_I = DEPTH;
    localparam integer ONE_I   = 1;

    localparam [AW-1:0] LAST    = LAST_I[AW-1:0];
    localparam [AW-1:0] PTR_ONE = ONE_I[AW-1:0];
    localparam [CW-1:0] DEPTH_C = DEPTH_I[CW-1:0];
    localparam [CW-1:0] CNT_ONE = ONE_I[CW-1:0];

    // Storage: datapath, not reset.
    reg [WIDTH-1:0] mem [0:DEPTH-1];

    reg [AW-1:0] wr_ptr;
    reg [AW-1:0] rd_ptr;
    reg [CW-1:0] count_q;

    // Flags: compares on a register only.
    assign full  = (count_q == DEPTH_C);
    assign empty = (count_q == {CW{1'b0}});
    assign count = count_q;

    // Accepted requests: the flags are the overflow/underflow policy.
    wire wr_acc = wr_en && !full;
    wire rd_acc = rd_en && !empty;

    // First-word fall-through read port.
    assign rd_data = mem[rd_ptr];

    // Storage write, only outside reset.
    always @(posedge clk) begin
        if (rst_n && wr_acc) begin
            mem[wr_ptr] <= wr_data;
        end
    end

    // Control: pointers and occupancy, synchronous active-low reset.
    always @(posedge clk) begin
        if (!rst_n) begin
            wr_ptr  <= {AW{1'b0}};
            rd_ptr  <= {AW{1'b0}};
            count_q <= {CW{1'b0}};
        end else begin
            if (wr_acc) begin
                wr_ptr <= (wr_ptr == LAST) ? {AW{1'b0}} : (wr_ptr + PTR_ONE);
            end
            if (rd_acc) begin
                rd_ptr <= (rd_ptr == LAST) ? {AW{1'b0}} : (rd_ptr + PTR_ONE);
            end
            case ({wr_acc, rd_acc})
                2'b10:   count_q <= count_q + CNT_ONE;
                2'b01:   count_q <= count_q - CNT_ONE;
                default: count_q <= count_q;
            endcase
        end
    end

`ifdef FORMAL
    // Design-intent assertions (not exercised by this task: no .sby submitted).
    reg f_past_valid = 1'b0;
    reg f_rst_seen   = 1'b0;

    always @(posedge clk) begin
        f_past_valid <= 1'b1;
        if (!rst_n) begin
            f_rst_seen <= 1'b1;
        end
    end

    always @(*) begin
        if (f_rst_seen) begin
            assert (full  == (count_q == DEPTH_C));
            assert (empty == (count_q == {CW{1'b0}}));
            assert (!(full && empty));
            assert (count_q <= DEPTH_C);
            assert (wr_ptr <= LAST);
            assert (rd_ptr <= LAST);
        end
    end

    always @(posedge clk) begin
        if (f_past_valid && f_rst_seen) begin
            if ($past(!rst_n)) begin
                assert (empty);
                assert (!full);
                assert (count_q == {CW{1'b0}});
                assert (wr_ptr == {AW{1'b0}});
                assert (rd_ptr == {AW{1'b0}});
            end else begin
                if ($past(wr_acc) && !$past(rd_acc)) begin
                    assert (count_q == $past(count_q) + CNT_ONE);
                end
                if (!$past(wr_acc) && $past(rd_acc)) begin
                    assert (count_q == $past(count_q) - CNT_ONE);
                end
                if ($past(wr_acc) == $past(rd_acc)) begin
                    assert (count_q == $past(count_q));
                end
                if ($past(wr_en && full)) begin
                    assert (wr_ptr == $past(wr_ptr));
                end
                if ($past(rd_en && empty)) begin
                    assert (rd_ptr == $past(rd_ptr));
                end
            end
        end
    end
`endif

endmodule

`default_nettype wire
=== END FILE ===
